/-!
# The prime-to-three quotient of the native HS centralizer

Two explicit elements of the actual central-involution centralizer generate
it, and the first has cube one. Five checked word identities recover the
three marked Sylow generators and the two marked generators of its S₅
quotient. The Sylow subgroup contains the entire pair kernel, so these
identities prove generation of the full centralizer. Its prime-to-three
quotient is consequently generated by the second element and is cyclic.

Sylow-center conjugacy transports this conclusion to every two-central
involution, retaining its actual centralizer and residual. The internal
imports reuse the native word and quotient witnesses without changing their
public interfaces. GAP discovers the words; all identities are checked on
the original 100 permutation letters by Lean's kernel.

Source: the HS inspection in Aschbacher–Smith 12.6.12, pp.825–826, and
GLS3 Table 5.3m. The native ATLAS carrier attribution is unchanged.
-/

public section
open Subgroup Theory.GroupTheory Theory.GroupTheory.DoubleCoverCentralizer
namespace CFSG.Quasithin.Chapter12.Section06.OriginalHigmanSimsNative
open Sporadic.LeechRelated.HS
open EvenLocalCandidates BlockNormalizer
